      "problem": "Find the point where the line $5x -4y=-8$ intersects the $y$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the $y$-intercept, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation and solve for $y.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-4y & =-8 \\\\ 5(0)-4y & =-8 \\\\ -4y & =-8 \\\\ y & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $2,$ and we conclude that the line intersects the $y$-axis at $\\left(0,2\\right).$",
